      <activity id="24a30778-09d6-525e-b349-3bc42bb78797" activityNameId="14692284-e2e7-5157-ae83-66d14d4aa183" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Industrial residue wood, softwood, plant-debarked, u=70%, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Industrial residue wood, softwood, plant-debarked, u=70%, at plant
The volume refers to the wood not including the bark. The multi-output process "sawing / debarking, softwood, at plant delivers the three coproducts "sawn timber, softwood, raw, plant-debarked, u=70%, at plant", "industrial residue wood, softwood, plant-debarked, u=70%, at plant" and "bark chips, softwood, u=140%, at plant". Allocation is based on the over-all proceeds of the process.;
UUID: 3b109d35-a30e-3945-8a4c-ded640d75646
Includes transports from forest, sawing, and debarking at sawmill.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Technology mix used in Germany 1986
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: The assumption that Germany is representative for central Europe is considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3b109d35-a30e-3945-8a4c-ded640d75646.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
